{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T69RmJdS1NQ2NysMrMvMSU","type":"tool_result","content":"paper_framing.md:39:**Existing approaches & gaps**: Behavioral GRPO decomposition (\"Pressure, What Pressure?\") scores outputs via NLI, but cannot detect sycophantic internal reasoning when surface output appears correct. ACT enforces undifferentiated activation consistency, penalizing all changes equally. Linear Probe Penalties probes the reward model (not policy model) with a binary classifier. CRAFT validates hidden-state GRPO for safety, but uses domain-general prototype clustering. All are single-turn.\npaper_framing.md:65:[Omitted long matching line]\ndecisions.yaml:163:    2. CRAFT 对比缺失 → 至少需 dedicated paragraph，理想加实验\nartifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T125925/best/paper_framing.md:27:**Existing approaches & gaps**: Behavioral GRPO decomposition (\"Pressure, What Pressure?\") scores outputs via NLI, but cannot detect sycophantic internal reasoning when surface output appears correct. ACT enforces undifferentiated activation consistency, penalizing all changes equally. Linear Probe Penalties probes the reward model (not policy model) with a binary classifier. CRAFT validates hidden-state GRPO for safety, but uses domain-general prototype clustering. All are single-turn.\nartifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T125925/best/paper_framing.md:36:- **Reviewer concern 1 (novelty)**: \"This is just RepE/CRAFT applied to sycophancy.\" Counter: (a) d_syc is explicitly positioned as a RepE application; the novelty is using it as a continuous GRPO reward signal, not the direction extraction itself; (b) multi-turn calibration with evidence-strength stratification and direction transfer are standalone contributions; (c) neither CRAFT nor RepE has been applied to the sycophancy-revision double-bind in training.\nartifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T125925/best/paper.tex:54:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/IDEA_BRIEF.md:188:[Omitted long 